sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2024-anthrobots-14> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Anthrobot behaviour and morphology are significantly associated: non-moving bots fall mostly in morphotype 1 (small, smooth, spherical), linear movers mostly in morphotype 2 (large, non-polarized cilia) and circular movers mostly in morphotype 3 (polarized cilia), and no displacing bot was found in morphotype 1.";
    dc:type "experimental-result";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Non-movers, linear and circular bots map onto morphotypes 1, 2 and 3";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Gumuskaya G, Srivastava P, Cooper BG, Lesser H, Semegran B, Garnier S, Levin M, “Motile Living Biobots Self-Construct from Adult Human Somatic Progenitor Seed Cells”, Advanced science (Weinheim, Baden-Wurttemberg, Germany) (2024), doi:10.1002/advs.202303575; section “Results › Distinct Movement Types and Morphotypes are Highly Correlated”. Scope: NHBE-derived Anthrobots; 350 imaged bots of which 28 had assigned displacing movement types"
}
